{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections","id":941643,"title":"Help me understand some uses of sympatetic connections","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-01T20:31:51-07:00","id":941643,"title":"Help me understand some uses of sympatetic connections","content":"There are two cases where i dont know if how i want to use sympatetic connections is alrigth.<br /> 1) Can i use people as sympatetic links?<br /> For instance, using guy to cast a spell on all his family and close friends<br /> 2)Can i cast magic through people or objects to affect other people?<br /> A stranger is wearing a ring very special to the character, so i use the intimate relationship to the ring to cast a curse on the man. Or my sleepwalker reteiner is meeting a seer and i use him to cast a mind reading spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:40:02-07:00","id":941678,"title":"","content":"My best interpretation is:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, you can use a person as a sympathetic yantra. They will usually have sympathetic connections to relatives.<br /> <br /> 2. Sympathetic spells need to focus on their target. You could cast a spell on the ring or the retainer, like Scrying, and then cast through the scrying window on your target of interest, but you couldn't, say, use a sympathetic yantra of the retainer to target the person they're talking to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:49:58-07:00","id":941731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=941678#post941678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My best interpretation is:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, you can use a person as a sympathetic yantra. They will usually have sympathetic connections to relatives.<br /> <br /> 2. Sympathetic spells need to focus on their target. You could cast a spell on the ring or the retainer, like Scrying, and then cast through the scrying window on your target of interest, but you couldn't, say, use a sympathetic yantra of the retainer to target the person they're talking to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is untrue actually. Sympathetic connections and Sympathetic Yantras are two different things. While it is possible that a Sympathetic Yantra has a Sympathetic Connection to the target (even if not required), the other way around is mostly false. This originates from the fact that Sympathetic Yantras are actually symbols of the subject you want to cast on. They have to represent the target itself, not anything or anyone connectect to the target.<br /> <br /> So for the questions:<br /> 1) No you cannot. What you CAN do is borrowing the Sympathetic Connections of a person to his family and then use that connections to cast a spell through it. You still need a Sympathetic Yantra, a family portrait e.g., to be able to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> 2) Again: no. You actually never can cast &quot;through&quot; anyone. You always need to have the connection yourself. So the scrying method works via &quot;Casting via Remote Viewing&quot; but otherwise not. What you could do is cast a spell on the ring, so that the wearer of the ring gets cursed somehow. But that wouldn't even need space magic if you got the ring at your disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-02-2016, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:22:07-07:00","id":941745,"title":"","content":"Hannes has the right of it - the Sympathetic Range attainment is clear that it works based off of the caster's sympathetic connection to the target. Thankfully, borrowing connections is easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:54:57-07:00","id":941762,"title":"","content":"The more difficult part is to actually know what connections to borrow. If you don't really know what connections a subject has and which ones you want to use, you have to do a lot of research to do on the subject via Correspondance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:25:49-07:00","id":942004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=941731#post941731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is untrue actually. Sympathetic connections and Sympathetic Yantras are two different things. While it is possible that a Sympathetic Yantra has a Sympathetic Connection to the target (even if not required), the other way around is mostly false. This originates from the fact that Sympathetic Yantras are actually symbols of the subject you want to cast on. They have to represent the target itself, not anything or anyone connectect to the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this, you are correct, I will concede. However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=941731#post941731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You always need to have the connection yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I'd not heard suggested until now (specifically, the idea that you need to borrow sympathetic threads beforehand. I'd always interpreted the idea that you need a sympathetic connection as allowing for you to use something else that has that connection as a part of your casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:32:56-07:00","id":942156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=941731#post941731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is untrue actually. Sympathetic connections and Sympathetic Yantras are two different things. While it is possible that a Sympathetic Yantra has a Sympathetic Connection to the target (even if not required), the other way around is mostly false. This originates from the fact that Sympathetic Yantras are actually symbols of the subject you want to cast on. They have to represent the target itself, not anything or anyone connectect to the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, i can use the blood of someone as a Sympathetic Yantras but not his father?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:46:29-07:00","id":942168,"title":"","content":"You can use his blood or his father but you still need a personal sympathetic connection to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:20:35-07:00","id":942193,"title":"","content":"Can't you use the sympathetic connection the blood has to him? You can outright open your stanky old wizard eyes and have a look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:23:42-07:00","id":942195,"title":"","content":"1. Kidnap his father.<br /> 2. Use Interconnections on his father.<br /> 3. Localize Sympathetic Connection you need.<br /> 4. Borrow it using Borrowing the Thread spell.<br /> 5. Design a spell.<br /> 6. It needs a Sympathetic Yantra: SACRIFICE HIS FATHER TO THE EYE<br /> 7. It needs you to have a Sympathetic Connection to the target; you borrowed it from the Father.<br /> 8. Finish the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:31:14-07:00","id":942202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942193#post942193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you use the sympathetic connection the blood has to him? You can outright open your stanky old wizard eyes and have a look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can use the sympathetic connection of the blood if you use a spell to borrow it's connection to him so you have a personal connection to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:32:54-07:00","id":942205,"title":"","content":"Why does the connection need to be attached to you? I mean, it's clearly not a huge extra step here but why is it required at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:39:34-07:00","id":942213,"title":"","content":"&quot; The <br /> spell is Withstood by the fragility of the sympathetic connection <br /> (p.173), between the mage and her subject&quot;<br /> Sympathetic Magic description. Seems to imply that it has to be attached. Not sure, not a fan of sympathetic magic so I don't know it that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:45:46-07:00","id":942218,"title":"","content":"The description of sympathy in the Space chapter mentions it functioning via routing the spells through the lines of sympathy, so it seems... I don't know. Conflicting?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> would probably be the person to consult on this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:54:08-07:00","id":942222,"title":"","content":"Dave is the reason I know that's what Borrow Sympathy is for, he talked about it ages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:57:29-07:00","id":942225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942218#post942218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of sympathy in the Space chapter mentions it functioning via routing the spells through the lines of sympathy, so it seems... I don't know. Conflicting?</div> </div> </div> </div>My go-to interpretation is that using sympathy is subject to the same stipulation as conventional range \u2014 you can use your own sympathies or those of something you're touching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T14:39:19-07:00","id":942239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942222#post942222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave is the reason I know that's what Borrow Sympathy is for, he talked about it ages ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a link? Because I can easily see Borrow Sympathy being used as a &quot;I have this for later&quot; spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T14:49:33-07:00","id":942244,"title":"","content":"It makes early Sympathetic Bombings little harder, which is good. You need to sustain Borrow Sympathy and *then* cast a Sympathetic spells - on Low-Level Gnosis, this means you might be needing to Reach more --&gt; create bigger Paradox on the actual &quot;fuck you, got Sympathy&quot; spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:05:45-07:00","id":942255,"title":"","content":"That's never been a problem for my games before. I mean, right off the bat, a sympathetic bombing is pretty much impossible with Gnosis 1-2 anyway; you've got, at best, a Fraying spell. You could maybe hope to knock them unconscious while they're doing something dangerous.<br /> <br /> Actually in the... Sheesh, half a decade I've been playing Mage now, I've never had a player cast an offensive spell sympathetically, bar one very, <i>very</i> special circumstance (involving a False Demesne needing a route to dissipate down).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:24:26-07:00","id":942270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942239#post942239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a link? Because I can easily see Borrow Sympathy being used as a &quot;I have this for later&quot; spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, like I said it was ages ago. I'll dig a bit though, see if I can't turn it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:44:32-07:00","id":942287,"title":"","content":"Spells are always withstood by <b>your</b> level of sympathy to the subject; how good a representation of the the sympathetic yantra is doesn't do anything, because it doesn't provide its dice bonus when used to activate the Attainment.<br /> <br /> The way you do things like &quot;ahahahaha, I have a drop of your blood, so I can curse you from across the country&quot; is to cast <i>Borrow Threads</i> on the blood first, and then cast your spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:58:48-07:00","id":942295,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I found it! *Looks up.* &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T16:20:49-07:00","id":942311,"title":"","content":"Well, that settles that. Thanks Dave!<br /> <br /> Feels weird to have to do that extra step, still, but it's consistent, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T17:11:32-07:00","id":942332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942311#post942311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that settles that. Thanks Dave!<br /> <br /> Feels weird to have to do that extra step, still, but it's consistent, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my understanding, it has to do with the metaphysics of Sympathy. Spells aren't really &quot;sent through Sympathetic Connections&quot;. They're cast at Sensory range. A Mage with a Sympathetic Connection to a subject can &quot;sense&quot; that subject in a manner of speaking, even if she can't see, hear, smell, or feel him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:26:23-07:00","id":942525,"title":"","content":"I agree with Charlaquin on this. In the moment you actually form the imago for the spell, you need some kind of connection sensory or sympathetic to the target to be able to imagine the spell hitting that target. If you don't have any, you cannot cast the spell. Describing this as sensing the target works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942168#post942168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use his blood or his father but you still need a personal sympathetic connection to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition, I think you actually cannot use anyones father as a Sympathetic Yantra. The Yantra has to be a representation of the subject itself. Familiy relation is not enough. The father can only represent himself and not his children.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:17:38-07:00","id":942905,"title":"","content":"That new gap actually makes for an interesting space for legacy attainment:<br /> An attainment that lets you reflexively borrow sympathy would be a great 1st optional Space for something like Fangs of Mara. Fine if that's limited to Mind and legacy attainments, though.<br /> <br /> Other legacies might treat certain things like the person for certain forms of magic. Tamers of Blood could have the ability to treat a blood sample as the entire pattern for Sympathy. Bokor might treat any parts of the body as the body, in similar way. Tremere might have a branch that can treat a soulstone as the soul itself, becoming able to wrest a soul remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:20:02-07:00","id":942908,"title":"","content":"Soulstone already gives you Connected Connection, which - amongst other things - makes any spell you cast at the subject using it automatically bypass Withstand. Yeahhhhhhhhhh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:59:39-07:00","id":942975,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> I have no idea what you're talking about, if you have the blood you -can- target the whole Pattern. You're not restricted to affecting the target's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T00:37:01-07:00","id":943473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942908#post942908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soulstone already gives you Connected Connection, which - amongst other things - makes any spell you cast at the subject using it automatically bypass Withstand. Yeahhhhhhhhhh.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's consistent, it's still a sympathetic spell. Assuming you know the subject's name, spend a mana, and use a Sympathy Yantra slot, it isn't Withstood at that point, but that's hardly the same as being the same as direct casting. That whole needing to borrow the connection thing would still apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}